{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q25102177","formula":"C₁₁H₁₂N₂O","hill":"C11H12N2O","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":11.0,"H":12.0,"N":2.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"Indolepropionamide"},"descriptions":{"en":"Indolepropionamide (IPAM) is a chemical compound, an indole derivative with the molecular formula C11H12N2O. In vivo (rats), IPAM markedly reduced the proton potential collapse induced by the mitochondrial toxins to nearly baseline levels in both young and old rats and demonstrated free-radical scavenging properties. IPAM was shown to increase complex I and complex IV activity in the mitochondrial electron transport chain, however complex II and complex III were left unchanged. Decreased activity of complexes I and IV results in an inhibition of electron transport that is associated with higher production of ROS."},"fame":3,"pubchemCid":351791,"mass":188.23,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=CC=C2C(=C1)C(=CN2)CCC(=O)N","inchikey":"OTVHXWFANORBAK-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"3-(1H-indol-3-yl)propanamide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"351791","atoms":26,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-4.128,"y":0.414,"z":1.025,"el":"O"},{"x":1.718,"y":-2.003,"z":-0.223,"el":"N"},{"x":-4.478,"y":0.64,"z":-1.236,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.05,"y":-0.789,"z":0.35,"el":"C"},{"x":1.063,"y":0.086,"z":0.206,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.427,"y":-0.408,"z":0.723,"el":"C"},{"x":2.159,"y":-0.701,"z":-0.154,"el":"C"},{"x":0.385,"y":-2.067,"z":0.08,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.303,"y":-0.073,"z":-0.497,"el":"C"},{"x":1.243,"y":1.476,"z":0.347,"el":"C"},{"x":3.432,"y":-0.164,"z":-0.381,"el":"C"},{"x":2.51,"y":2.027,"z":0.123,"el":"C"},{"x":3.587,"y":1.217,"z":-0.235,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.712,"y":0.345,"z":-0.128,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.407,"y":0.452,"z":1.405,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.896,"y":-1.222,"z":1.29,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.134,